{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_2>\nimport itertools\nimport bisect\n\nn, m = map(int, input().split())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\ndef get_modular_sums(arr, mod):\n    res = []\n    for r in range(len(arr)+1):\n        for comb in itertools.combinations(arr, r):\n            res.append(sum(comb) % mod)\n    return res\n\nn1 = n // 2\na1_mods = get_modular_sums(a[:n1], m)\na2_mods = get_modular_sums(a[n1:], m)\n\na1_unique_sorted = sorted(set(a1_mods))\n\ndef find_best_pair(x):\n    target = m - x\n    idx = bisect.bisect_left(a1_unique_sorted, target)\n    if idx == 0:\n        return x\n    return a1_unique_sorted[idx-1] + x\n\nresults = [find_best_pair(val) for val in a2_mods]\nprint(max(results))\n</your_rewritten_code_2>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] firstLine = br.readLine().split(\" \");\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(firstLine[0]);\n        int m = Integer.parseInt(firstLine[1]);\n        \n        String[] secondLine = br.readLine().split(\" \");\n        int[] a = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            a[i] = Integer.parseInt(secondLine[i]);\n        }\n        \n        int n1 = n / 2;\n        List<Integer> a1_mods = getModularSums(a, 0, n1, m);\n        List<Integer> a2_mods = getModularSums(a, n1, n - n1, m);\n        \n        Set<Integer> a1Set = new HashSet<>(a1_mods);\n        List<Integer> a1UniqueSorted = new ArrayList<>(a1Set);\n        Collections.sort(a1UniqueSorted);\n        \n        List<Integer> results = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int val : a2_mods) {\n            results.add(findBestPair(val, a1UniqueSorted, m));\n        }\n        \n        int maxResult = Collections.max(results);\n        System.out.println(maxResult);\n    }\n    \n    private static List<Integer> getModularSums(int[] arr, int start, int length, int mod) {\n        List<Integer> res = new ArrayList<>();\n        int[] elements = new int[length];\n        for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\n            elements[i] = arr[start + i];\n        }\n        \n        int n = length;\n        for (int r = 0; r <= n; r++) {\n            int[] combination = new int[r];\n            combine(elements, 0, 0, r, combination, res, mod);\n        }\n        \n        return res;\n    }\n    \n    private static void combine(int[] arr, int start, int index, int r, int[] combination, List<Integer> res, int mod) {\n        if (index == r) {\n            int sum = 0;\n            for (int i = 0; i < r; i++) {\n                sum += combination[i];\n            }\n            res.add(sum % mod);\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        for (int i = start; i < arr.length; i++) {\n            combination[index] = arr[i];\n            combine(arr, i + 1, index + 1, r, combination, res, mod);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    private static int findBestPair(int x, List<Integer> sortedList, int m) {\n        int target = m - x;\n        int idx = Collections.binarySearch(sortedList, target);\n        if (idx < 0) {\n            idx = -idx - 1;\n        }\n        \n        if (idx == 0) {\n            return x;\n        }\n        \n        return sortedList.get(idx - 1) + x;\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001234931987710297, -2.861018856492592e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.00014423283573705703, -2.1815061700181104e-05, -0.01603645831346512, -0.25217169523239136, -0.0025009801611304283, -1.2874520507466514e-05, -0.0003746046277228743, -0.000270091783022508, -8.702239938429557e-06, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -0.0004663571889977902, -0.0019302800064906478, -0.000382707774406299, -0.0059755961410701275, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -0.01282067596912384, -0.0019378946162760258, -4.768370445162873e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.6331539882230572e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.07892808318138123, -0.0036457993555814028, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -9.727005090098828e-05, -0.00020549570035655051, -5.960462772236497e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -7.748573807475623e-06, -8.702239938429557e-06, -1.597391747054644e-05, -2.312633478140924e-05, -1.6093124941107817e-05, -2.753696753643453e-05, -1.9311717551317997e-05, -0.0014373458689078689, -2.264974000354414e-06, -0.7217446565628052, -3.790783375734463e-05, 0.0, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -1.1205610462639015e-05, 0.0, -6.353653589030728e-05, -0.00016080040950328112, -2.7656173188006505e-05, -1.728519782773219e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -3.4450891689630225e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.9192511899746023e-05, -1.7881377516459906e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -3.814689989667386e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -2.7418097943154862e-06, 0.0, -5.006777428206988e-06, -1.7881377516459906e-06